Ques9: Compare:
(a). GPS vs Optical Flow
               GPS
→ Use satellites to find location.
→ Works best outdoors.
              Optical Flow
→ Uses a camera to track ground movement.
→ Works best indoors or at low height.
(b). LiDAR vs Ultrasonic:
              LiDAR
→ Uses laser beams.
→ More accurate and long range.
              Ultrasonic
→ Uses sound waves.
→ Less accurate and short range.
(c). Gyroscope vs Accelerometer:
               Gyroscope
→ Measure rotation.
→ Controls roll, pitch, and yaw.
                Accelerometer
→ Measures acceleration and tilt.
→ Helps maintain balance and detects movement.
